    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0527" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2629</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1916, noon</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 25, 8 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3800. There is a quiet conflict on between Military and Navy on one side and many
                    sincere Germans on the other side who advocate a decent conduct of submarine
                    war. Last number of Maximilian Harden’s magazine entitled <hi
                        rendition="#italic">If I Were Wilson </hi> has just been confiscated <pb
                        facs="0528" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/> by military authorities. It had been on
                    sale some days and in it Harden claimed that the President was right and had
                    only made proper claims against Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
